```sql
--Description / Thinking process:
-- Goal: preview how each Nature article body will be tokenised for later vector work.
-- Steps:
--   1. Select from WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE (source articles).
--   2. Lower‑case the "body" text so tokens are case‑insensitive.
--   3. Replace every non‑alphabetic character with a space via REGEXP_REPLACE,
--      giving a clean sequence of letters and spaces.
--   4. Use SPLIT(cleaned_body,' ') to turn that string into an array of substrings.
--   5. FLATTEN the array with a LATERAL clause so each token appears on its own row.
--   6. Re‑clean each token (remove any residual non‑letters) and force lower‑case.
--   7. Filter out very short tokens (<3 chars) which are often undesired.
--   8. Return article "id", "title", and a sample "token" to verify the pipeline.
--   9. LIMIT 20 so the result set is small and quick.
SELECT
    n."id",
    n."title",
    LOWER(REGEXP_REPLACE(tok.value::STRING, '[^a-zA-Z]', '')) AS "token"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE n,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(
         INPUT => SPLIT(
             REGEXP_REPLACE(LOWER(n."body"), '[^a-zA-Z]+', ' '),
             ' '
         )
     ) tok
WHERE n."body" IS NOT NULL          -- ensure body exists
  AND LENGTH(tok.value::STRING) >= 3 -- discard very short tokens
LIMIT 20;
```
