Ten exploratory Snowflake queries (all limited to 20 rows, each enclosed
column name in double quotes, and growing from very simple to multi‑table):

```sql
-- 1) Quick look at a handful of Nature records
-- Description: Inspect primary identifiers, dates and titles.
SELECT
    "id",
    "date",
    "title"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Peek at article bodies containing the term ‘autism’
-- Description: Example fuzzy search to gauge how autism appears in text.
SELECT
    "id",
    "title",
    LEFT("body", 500) AS "body_snippet"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE
WHERE "body" ILIKE '%autism%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Review distinct category values present
-- Description: Helps discover categories for possible focused queries.
SELECT DISTINCT
    "category"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Obtain overall word frequencies for a few key tokens
-- Description: Fetch frequencies that will be used for 0.4‑power weighting.
SELECT
    "word",
    "frequency"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_FREQUENCIES
WHERE "word" IN ('epigenetics', 'cerebral', 'organoids', 'autism')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Grab the raw GloVe vector for the word ‘autism’
-- Description: Shows vector structure in the VARIANT column.
SELECT
    "word",
    "vector"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.GLOVE_VECTORS
WHERE "word" = 'autism'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Sample join: words with both a frequency and a GloVe vector
-- Description: Demonstrates how to intersect the two reference tables.
SELECT
    f."word",
    f."frequency",
    g."vector"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_FREQUENCIES  f
JOIN WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.GLOVE_VECTORS     g
      ON f."word" = g."word"
WHERE f."word" IN ('epigenetics', 'autism')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) List Nature papers that mention either ‘epigenetic’ or ‘organoid’
-- Description: Narrow article subset that will likely score higher later.
SELECT
    "id",
    "date",
    "title"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE
WHERE "body" ILIKE '%epigenetic%'
   OR "body" ILIKE '%organoid%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Inspect keywords field for potential filtering words
-- Description: Some Nature records embed useful tokens inside keywords.
SELECT
    "id",
    "keywords"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE
WHERE "keywords" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Count Nature rows with a non‑null body (sanity check for processing)
-- Description: Ensures body text exists before heavy vector computation.
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS "rows_with_body"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE
WHERE "body" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) (More complex) Pull candidate articles, plus pre‑tokenised words
-- Description: Tokenise body into lower‑case words (simple regex split)
--              keep only alphabetic tokens ≥3 chars, flatten the array so
--              each word is on its own row; ready to join frequency/vector.
SELECT
    n."id",
    n."title",
    LOWER(REGEXP_REPLACE(word.value::STRING, '[^a-zA-Z]', '')) AS "token"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE n,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(
         REGEXP_SPLIT(LOWER(n."body"), '[^a-zA-Z]+')
     ) word
WHERE n."body" IS NOT NULL
  AND LENGTH(word.value::STRING) >= 3
LIMIT 20;
```

